<title>USA: Raychem sets two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>Raychem sets two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raychem Corp said Friday its board of directors have approved a two-for-one stock split, subject to shareholder approval.</p>
<p>If approved by Raychem's stockholders at the company's upcoming annual meeting, the two-for-one stock split and increase in authorized capital stock would become effective upon the amendment of Raychem's certificate of incorporation.</p>
<p>At the end of June Raychem had about 44.6 million shares outstanding.</p>
